"""
Propose top_genes / top_cat / top_num for every dataset-level .md.

Heuristics (best-judgment, tuned for neuro-immunology / AD focus):

  top_genes
    Pick a marker panel based on the dataset's cell type (from .h5ad.mus
    annotation), specialise it for disease context (e.g. AD → DAM + GWAS
    hits), then INTERSECT with the genes actually present in the
    accompanying .duckdb.  Mouse datasets use title-case lookup against the
    actual gene list (so genuine mouse spelling — P2ry12 — wins over the
    canonical human form).

  top_cat
    Walk a priority list (cluster/annotation > disease/condition >
    sample/donor > demographics > region) and pick the first 4 that exist
    in the dataset's obs.

  top_num
    Walk a priority list weighted towards module scores
    (starcat__*, anthive__*, WGCNA modules) over raw QC.  Pick first 4
    that exist.

By default the script SKIPS files that already have a populated top_genes
list — your existing curation isn't trampled.  Use --force to overwrite.

Usage:
  ant-suggest-tops [--all | --dry-run] [--force] [--glob PATH]

  --all       run against data/h5adstore/<group>/<file>.md (default)
  --dry-run   print what would change but don't write
  --force     overwrite even when top_* fields are already populated
  --glob      restrict to a path glob (e.g. 'Blackburn2026/*.md')
"""

